  closure census over all bases: Z_3: 6/6, Z_4: 6/6, Z_5: 4/6, Z_6: 6/6, Z_7: 3/6, Z_8: 2/6, Z_9: 6/6
  total stack sums of the six bases: [9, 12, 12, 15, 15, 18] - ALL divisible by 3
  -> Z_3 is the SMALLEST code closing every minimal chiral base
     (Z_4, Z_6, Z_9 also close all six at this scope), and the
     mechanism is visible: every minimal base's total charge is
     divisible by 3, so the full stack itself is the closing
     triple.  A triality-flavored hint (QCD's center is Z_3),
     reported as a Phase-I observation at stated scope, NOT a
     derivation.

== verdict accounting ==
  Z_6, k = 6: raw 44100 -> anomaly 282 -> chiral 72 -> closure 72 -> generations 0
  -> Phase I outputs three structure theorems for (M):
     (1) no chiral matter below base size 3 (P14, used);
     (2) generations factorize through the anomaly filter:
         minimal 3-generation chiral content = 9 + 9;
     (3) the closure census selects small triality-friendly
         codes.  The search is a bounded enumeration now.
